#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186380873 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129171 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "307bccb6-036f-51bb-99ce-327aad8dfdbe" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Double Integral When the Integrand Contains Only One Variable"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a2b5bd46-9ad9-5287-8540-de4fec5b349c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380875} {:answer/id #uuid "f9b9919a-def8-55b0-b9c2-b44fc832ab35" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "14" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380876} {:answer/id #uuid "831f7c88-e098-5c1f-a8e5-ccb34b89df28" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380877} {:answer/id #uuid "67ea11e1-25b5-553f-9220-1d54bd8cbd08" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "32" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380878} {:answer/id #uuid "14b66f59-cdaf-5100-99dd-152700887b12" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380879}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "14b66f59-cdaf-5100-99dd-152700887b12" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380879} :answer-field/id #uuid "4f5de000-5e2e-5293-bbbc-fea0dfb73f12" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380874}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "2a641d94-d436-5610-8401-c196fdb866a7" :question/math-academy-id "q-129953" :question/problem "Calculate ${∬}_{R}(3{x}^{2}+6{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}A$,  where $R=[-1,0]\\times [0,2].$" :question/worked-solution "Using the linearity property of double integrals, we can write\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{R}(3{x}^{2}+6{y}^{2})\\text{d}A & ={∬}_{R}3{x}^{2}\\text{ }\\text{d}A+{∬}_{R}6{y}^{2}\\text{ }\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe function under the first integral is independent of $y.$ So, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{R}3{x}^{2}\\text{ }\\text{d}A & =(2-0){\\int }_{-1}^{0}3{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2({x}^{3}{|}_{-1}^{0}) \\\\  & =2({0}^{3}-(-1)^{3}) \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe function under the second integral is independent of $x.$ So, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{R}6{y}^{2}\\text{ }\\text{d}A & =(0-(-1)){\\int }_{0}^{2}6{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =2{y}^{3}{|}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =2\\cdot {2}^{3}-0 \\\\  & =16.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, combining our results, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{R}(3{x}^{2}+6{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}A=2+16=18.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186380894 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129188 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8505beff-75b8-57bf-9312-e0fcf32f44fd" :knowledge-point/title "Using Additivity of Double Integrals"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a2e15614-cf10-5035-a3e9-1e74b5a8b0de" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{∬}_{S\\cup T}(\\frac{x}{y}+{x}^{2}-x{y}^{3})\\text{d}A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380896} {:answer/id #uuid "d9b88361-c3e7-5541-acf8-ca9ffbbb62e2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{∬}_{S\\cup T}\\frac{x}{y}({x}^{2}-x{y}^{3})\\,\\text{d}A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380897} {:answer/id #uuid "180eeba2-deb2-5cf1-b167-3418a77c6df3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{∬}_{S}\\frac{x}{y}\\,\\text{d}A+{∬}_{U}({x}^{2}-x{y}^{3})\\,\\text{d}A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380898} {:answer/id #uuid "92d66543-c3a6-5f98-bd86-be2ec63d6e7a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{∬}_{S}\\frac{x}{y}\\,\\text{d}A+{∬}_{T}({x}^{2}-x{y}^{3})\\,\\text{d}A+{∬}_{U}\\,\\text{d}A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380899} {:answer/id #uuid "5e937bea-7600-5aff-bb43-6733c9d40198" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{∬}_{S}\\frac{x}{y}\\,\\text{d}A+{∬}_{T}({x}^{2}-x{y}^{3})\\,\\text{d}A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380900}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5e937bea-7600-5aff-bb43-6733c9d40198" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{∬}_{S}\\frac{x}{y}\\,\\text{d}A+{∬}_{T}({x}^{2}-x{y}^{3})\\,\\text{d}A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380900} :answer-field/id #uuid "e64f7bef-5384-5c7a-9b11-57463fc18d7e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380895}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "9798be4b-01fe-51e0-b1bf-171e60296bfd" :question/math-academy-id "q-130023" :question/problem "![](images/e5/e50797d61a59cf8533e86695c03da168bff7e59ce363e0ee42bb700de515385f.png)\n\nConsider the region $R$ shown above. Let the function $f(x,y)$ be defined as\n\n$$\nf(x,y)={\\begin{aligned}\\frac{x}{y}, & (x,y)\\in S, \\\\ {x}^{2}-x{y}^{3}, & (x,y)\\in T, \\\\ 0, & (x,y)\\in U.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen,\n\n$$\n{∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\text{ }\\text{d}A=\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that the domain $R$ can be represented as a union of three sub-domains, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R & =S\\cup T\\cup U.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we can write\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A & ={∬}_{S}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A+{∬}_{T}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A+{∬}_{U}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{S}\\frac{x}{y}\\,\\text{d}A+{∬}_{T}({x}^{2}-x{y}^{3})\\,\\text{d}A+{∬}_{U}0\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{S}\\frac{x}{y}\\,\\text{d}A+{∬}_{T}({x}^{2}-x{y}^{3})\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129